  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "When two simultaneous transactions update the same object(s), the second transaction should fail at commit time, preferably before any of its changes are persisted. This failure should produce a 409 status on the commit.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "A few notes on how this may work:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "The OCFL java client includes mechanisms for optimistic locking based on the expected Head version number at the time of committing",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "OCFLObjectSession includes the unimplemented ",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "marks": [
            {
             "type": "strong"
            }
           ],
           "text": "prepare()",
           "type": "text"
          },
          {
           "text": " method.",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        },
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "content": [
            {
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "This method could perform a precheck and lock on objects it is updating",
               "type": "text"
              }
             ],
             "type": "paragraph"
            }
           ],
           "type": "listItem"
          },
          {
           "content": [
            {
             "content": [
              {
               "text": "We would most likely need to capture the current head version per ocfl object when they are first modified, for checking later against the head version in OCFL.",
               "type": "text"
              }
             ],
             "type": "paragraph"
            }
           ],
           "type": "listItem"
          }
         ],
         "type": "bulletList"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": " ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Should be able to update/reenable/replace integration test:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/TransactionsIT.java#L414"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/TransactionsIT.java#L414",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
