  "description": "<p>When two simultaneous transactions update the same object(s), the second transaction should fail at commit time, preferably before any of its changes are persisted. This failure should produce a 409 status on the commit.</p>\n\n<p>A few notes on how this may work:</p>\n<ul>\n\t<li>The OCFL java client includes mechanisms for optimistic locking based on the expected Head version number at the time of committing</li>\n\t<li>OCFLObjectSession includes the unimplemented <b>prepare()</b> method.\n\t<ul>\n\t\t<li>This method could perform a precheck and lock on objects it is updating</li>\n\t\t<li>We would most likely need to capture the current head version per ocfl object when they are first modified, for checking later against the head version in OCFL.</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Should be able to update/reenable/replace integration test:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/TransactionsIT.java#L414\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo4/fcrepo4/blob/master/fcrepo-http-api/src/test/java/org/fcrepo/integration/http/api/TransactionsIT.java#L414</a></p>",
